+Thanks for contributing to `awesome-best-open-source-ai-automation-tools-2026`.
+
+## Submission Rules
+
+- Every tool must link to a public `github.com` repository.
+- No proprietary SaaS products, closed-source services, or hosted-only listings.
+- The repo must be clearly relevant to AI automation, agent tooling, workflow orchestration, MCP integrations, DevOps automation, or a closely related category.
+- Include the repository URL, stars, primary language, license, and why it belongs in the list.
+- Prefer active repositories with clear documentation.
+- If a category is thin, note the gap instead of forcing low-quality additions.
+
+## Pull Request Checklist
+
+Before opening a PR, make sure you:
+
+1. Verified the repository is public and currently accessible on GitHub.
+2. Confirmed the project is open source and not a docs-only or install-only repo.
+3. Added or updated metadata for stars, language, license, and last commit activity.
+4. Wrote a concise description that matches the repository’s README or GitHub description.
+5. Checked for duplicates or near-duplicates already in the list.
+
+## Suggested Entry Format
+
+Use this structure for new entries:
+
+```md
+#### [Tool Name](https://github.com/username/repo)
+> **Description:** Short summary of what the repo does, why it matters, and the relevant metadata context.
+
+- **GitHub:** [github.com/username/repo](https://github.com/username/repo)
+- **Stars:** 123 ⭐
+- **Language:** TypeScript
+- **License:** MIT
+- **Last Commit:** ![GitHub last commit](https://img.shields.io/github/last-commit/username/repo)
+- **Category:** tag1, tag2
+- **Best for:** specific use case
+```
+
+## Quality Bar
+
+This repo is curated, not exhaustive. Submissions may be declined if they are:
+
+- Off-topic
+- Duplicative
+- Low-signal
+- Archived or abandoned
+- Missing a valid GitHub repo URL
+
+## Reporting Issues
+
+Open an issue if:
+
+- A repository has been archived, renamed, or removed.
+- Metadata is outdated.
+- A category is misleading.
+- A listed tool is not actually open source.
