+## FAQ
+
+### What are the best open source AI automation tools for self-hosting in 2026?
+Projects like `harbor`, `OpenFlux`, `allama`, `buildship`, and `ai-agent-automation` are among the clearer self-hostable options in this list. The right choice depends on whether you want a workflow builder, a code-first stack, or a local operations-focused tool.
+
+### Which open source AI automation tools are best for MCP and agent tool use?
+If you need MCP support or tool exposure for AI assistants, start with `apify-mcp-server`, `connery-sdk`, `mcp-server-js`, `mcp-server-excel`, and `codebase-mcp`. These are more integration-oriented than end-user workflow platforms.
+
+### Are there open source alternatives to proprietary AI workflow automation SaaS?
+Yes. This list intentionally avoids proprietary SaaS tools and only includes public GitHub repositories. `buildship`, `OpenFlux`, `harbor`, and `langmanus` are examples of code-visible alternatives for teams that want more control.
+
+### Which GitHub repositories here are most relevant for developer automation?
+For engineering teams, `codescan`, `aidevops`, `ops0-cli`, `qwen_cli_coder`, and `reviewcerberus` are the strongest fits. They align with code analysis, DevOps execution, command automation, and review workflows.
+
+### How do I evaluate an open source AI automation tool before adopting it?
+Check the license, last commit activity, issue responsiveness, documentation depth, and whether the repo’s architecture matches your environment. For this reason, each entry includes stars, language, license, and a live last-commit badge.
+
+### Why are some popular AI projects missing from this awesome list?
+Because this repository is intentionally narrow. If a project did not resolve to a public GitHub repository, looked like a docs-only repo, or was not clearly an AI automation tool, it was excluded.
+
+### What if a category has very few open source GitHub repos?
+That is useful market information. This README documents thin categories honestly instead of filling them with marginal or off-topic repositories.
+
